---
import site from "../data/site.json";
const directorRole = site.safeguardingContact.role;
---

<section aria-labelledby="safeguarding-policy-heading">
  <h2 id="safeguarding-policy-heading">Our Child Safeguarding Policy</h2>
  <h3>Our commitment.</h3>
  <p>
    EAZY-IRA Charity Foundation works with children in Masoro, Kigali. Every
    child has the right to be safe, respected and protected from harm. Everyone
    who takes part in our activities, including founders, leaders, volunteers
    and visitors, must follow this policy.
  </p>

  <h3>How we protect children.</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Respect.</strong> We speak and act kindly. We never use physical punishment, insults, humiliation, favouritism or discrimination.</li>
    <li><strong>Never alone.</strong> No adult is alone with a child out of sight of others during Foundation activities. We use open, shared spaces. Home visits are made by at least two team members.</li>
    <li><strong>Photos and videos.</strong> We take and publish a child's photo or video only with the guardian's consent. We never publish a child's full name, home address or school. Guardians can withdraw consent at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Private information.</strong> We keep information about children and families private and share it only with people who need it to keep a child safe.</li>
    <li><strong>Gifts and contact.</strong> Adults do not give private gifts or money to children, and do not contact children privately by phone or social media. School items are given openly through the Foundation.</li>
    <li><strong>Volunteers.</strong> Everyone who works with children reads and agrees to this policy first, and new volunteers start by working alongside experienced team members.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>If you are worried about a child.</h3>
  <p>
    Tell our {directorRole} straight away:{" "}
    <a href={`tel:${site.phone.value.replaceAll(" ", "")}`}>{site.phone.value}</a>
    {" "}or <a href={`mailto:${site.email.value}`}>{site.email.value}</a>. If the
    concern is about the Director, tell another leader of the Foundation or
    call the child helpline directly. If a child is in immediate danger, call
    112. To report child abuse, call 116 (free, Rwanda National Police child
    helpline). The Isange One Stop Centre, 3029 (free), offers medical, legal
    and counselling support to children and others who have been abused.
  </p>

  <h3>What we do when a concern is raised.</h3>
  <p>
    We listen, we do not promise to keep it secret, and we write down what was
    said. The Director acts the same day to keep the child safe and works with
    the authorities where abuse is suspected. Nobody is punished for raising a
    concern in good faith.
  </p>

  <h3>Review.</h3>
  <p>Our leaders review this policy at least once a year.</p>
</section>
